/* book Worked example: Q: A closed theodolite traverse ABCD is run clockwise round the inside of a site to fix four control stations. The observed interior angles are B 95°35′20″, C 91°34′50″, D 84°13′20″ and A 88°37′10″. The bearing of AB is fixed at 48°20′00″ and A is at E 1000.000 m, N 2000.000 m. The lengths are AB 245.60, BC 198.35, CD 261.40 and DA 230.12 m. Adjust the angles, compute the bearings, the closing error and the relative precision, and find the adjusted coordinates of B, C and D by Bowditch's rule.
   1. Angle sum = 360°00′40″; for four stations it should be (2 × 4 − 4) × 90° = 360°. Error +40″, so subtract 10″ from each: B 95°35′10″, C 91°34′40″, D 84°13′10″, A 88°37′00″.
   2. Bearings: BC = 48°20′00″ + 180° − 95°35′10″ = 132°44′50″; CD = 132°44′50″ + 180° − 91°34′40″ = 221°10′10″; DA = 221°10′10″ + 180° − 84°13′10″ = 316°57′00″. Check: AB = 316°57′00″ + 180° − 88°37′00″ − 360° = 48°20′00″.
   3. Departures (l sin β) and latitudes (l cos β), in m: AB +183.47, +163.27; BC +145.66, −134.63; CD −172.08, −196.77; DA −157.09, +168.16. Sums: ΣDep = −0.04 m, ΣLat = +0.03 m, over Σl = 935.47 m.
   4. Closing error e = √(0.04² + 0.03²) = 0.05 m. Relative precision = 935.47 ÷ 0.05 = 1 in 18 700, better than 1 in 10 000, so the traverse is accepted.
   5. Bowditch corrections (per metre: departure +0.04 ÷ 935.47, latitude −0.03 ÷ 935.47): departures +0.011, +0.008, +0.011, +0.010 m; latitudes −0.008, −0.006, −0.009, −0.007 m (each column rounded so that it sums to the error).
   6. Adjusted departures and latitudes: AB +183.481, +163.262; BC +145.668, −134.636; CD −172.069, −196.779; DA −157.080, +168.153. Both columns now sum to zero.
   7. Coordinates: B = (1000.000 + 183.481, 2000.000 + 163.262) = (1183.481, 2163.262); C = (1329.149, 2028.626); D = (1157.080, 1831.847); and DA brings the traverse back to A (1000.000, 2000.000).
   Answer: Adjusted angles 95°35′10″, 91°34′40″, 84°13′10″, 88°37′00″; closing error 0.05 m, precision 1 in 18 700. Adjusted coordinates: B (1183.481, 2163.262), C (1329.149, 2028.626), D (1157.080, 1831.847) m. */
